    "explanation": "To the rider: the $6.00 no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-02705 is not refunded, and SGD 4.80 of it is paid to the driver as compensation.\n\nYour central argument — that the driver cancelled 76 seconds before the 480-second free waiting period had run, so POL-NS-06 requires a full refund — reads the arithmetic backwards. The driver entered the Changi T3 Arrival PHV bay geofence at 18:18:27 and held position there continuously until 18:27:43: a qualifying in-geofence run of 556 seconds on EV-GPS-02705 (57 qualifying fixes, 100% coverage, no gaps). The free waiting period in force for this trip, from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec, is 480 seconds. The driver therefore waited 76 seconds LONGER than required (556 − 480), not shorter — the derived shortfall figure of −76 seconds is a surplus, and the 18:27:44 cancellation fell well after the period had elapsed. POL-NS-06 does not apply and no refund is due on it. Your alternative framing, that only 555 seconds had passed since the wait timer started, is still more than 480 and fails on the same arithmetic.\n\nI have tested each limb of POL-NS-01 and all four hold: (a) the trip record carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 18:18:27; (b) the GPS trace places the driver inside the 150 m AIRPORT arrival radius at that same timestamp (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0), so the marker and the waiting clock coincide and there is no false-arrival gap for POL-NS-05 to catch; (c) the continuous in-geofence dwell of 556 seconds exceeds the 480-second waiting period; and (d) the driver terminated the trip at 18:27:44 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, with no boarding event, after the required dwell had elapsed. Nothing in POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee. POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) does not apply because the driver was inside the arrival radius, not outside it. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate you: you sent no locating or coordinating message during the waiting window — the only chat message is the driver's — and your own device never entered the 200 m AIRPORT rider-presence radius, remaining about 790 m from the pin throughout (min 789.3 m, mean 792.8 m, max 796.5 m), so limb (c) is affirmatively failed on your own track. The fare ledger reconciles to the policy fee ($6.00 charged equals platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of 6.00), so there is no integrity defect under POL-NS-08(d).\n\nTo the driver: you are paid SGD 4.80. Under POL-NS-07 the compensation is 80 percent of the $6.00 fee in force, the platform retaining the residual 20 percent. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 0 (below 4) and 0 divided by 57 completed_trips_30d is 0.00 (below 0.08), and both limbs must hold to withhold payment. The rider's own track corroborates your account that no rider appeared at the bay.\n\nOn a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling the amount_sgd mirrors the driver payment per POL-GEN-03: the rider's $6.00 charge stands and the ruling moves SGD 4.80. That figure is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold of POL-GEN-05. No referral is issued: POL-NS-05(ii) is not engaged because no false arrival was found, and no POL-NS-01 reason-code mis-selection occurred because RIDER_NO_SHOW is the correct code on these facts. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02705-01 (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) is not relied on — a single continuous 556-second run already meets the minimum, so no advisory-driven accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) is needed. No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is met: no admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence; there is no repeat-abuse pattern (0 disputes between these parties in 90 days; rider no_show_disputes_30d is 1); and the deciding evidence is unimpaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d), so the POL-GEN-02 cap rests on artifacts at full weight 1.0. Profile fields were used only as context."
  },
