    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the $6.00 no-show cancellation fee stands, and the driver is compensated SGD 4.80 out of it. Neither figure is a refund to the rider.\n\nWhy the fee is chargeable (POL-NS-01). The clause needs all four conditions and all four hold. (a) The trip record EV-TRIP-02705 carries a driver 'arrived' event at 18:18:27. (b) The GPS trace EV-GPS-02705 places the driver inside the AIRPORT arrival radius (150 m) from 18:18:27, the first qualifying in-geofence fix (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0), so the marker coincides with the arrival and is not a false marker under POL-NS-05. (c) The driver held position in the geofence continuously for 556 seconds over 57 qualifying fixes, from 18:18:27 to 18:27:43. The free waiting period in force is 480 seconds (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec, and fee_schedule minimum_dwell_sec for AIRPORT). The dwell therefore EXCEEDED the required minimum by 76 seconds — the computed shortfall_sec is -76.0, a negative shortfall, that is, a surplus. (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 18:27:44 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the dwell had elapsed, and no boarding event is recorded.\n\nThe rider's central claim is rejected. The Rider Advocate argued the dwell was 76 seconds SHORT of the 480-second minimum, so that POL-NS-06 requires a full refund. That claim reverses the sign of the measurement. A 556-second in-geofence run against a 480-second minimum is 76 seconds long, not short; the cancellation at 18:27:44 came 555 seconds after the 480-second wait timer started at 18:18:29, past the time required. There is no shortfall for POL-NS-06 to operate on. The MISSING advisory EV-ADVIS-02705-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) could only ever have let separate in-geofence intervals be summed; the driver's single continuous run needs no summing, so its absence changes nothing.\n\nThe rider's other claims are also rejected. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider: limb (a) requires a locating or coordinating message SENT BY THE RIDER, and the only message in EV-CHAT-02705 was sent by the driver at 18:18:57 ('which door are you at'); the rider sent none and never replied. Limb (c) also fails on the rider's own track EV-GPS-02705, which places her device about 790 m from the pin (min 789.3 m, mean 792.8 m) with zero qualifying fixes inside the 200 m AIRPORT rider-presence radius. POL-NS-03 does not apply because the driver's stationary fixes are inside the arrival radius, not outside it.\n\nThe driver's claims are accepted. The fare ledger EV-FARE-02705 shows the $6.00 cancellation-fee line and reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect; payment_status is CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so the charge stands.\n\nDriver compensation. Under POL-NS-07 the anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 0 (below the 4-or-more limb) and 0 divided by completed_trips_30d of 57 is 0.0 (below the 0.08 rate limb), and both limbs must hold to withhold. Compensation is therefore paid at 80% of the $6.00 fee = SGD 4.80. Because compensation is paid, the emitted ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, with amount_sgd mirroring driver_compensation_sgd as POL-GEN-03 requires; the $6.00 charge itself is unchanged.\n\nEscalation and referrals. No POL-NS-09 trigger is engaged: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, the artifacts agree with one another, both disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1 (below 3), and no deciding artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08 limbs (a) to (d). No clause in this category produces a referral on these facts, so the referrals list is empty.\n\nConfidence is 0.9. The deciding facts rest on EV-TRIP-02705, EV-GPS-02705, EV-FARE-02705 and EV-DPROF-02705, each at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and no discount applies."
  },
